  "notes": [
    "H2.2 comprises 5 role comparisons; each line reports the unadjusted p with the Benjamini-Hochberg adjusted value appended.",
    "A defensible way to state the finding is: the corpus that represents contemporary, actively maintained apps shows markedly higher coverage, and the residual debt in it is the quantity that matters for agents today."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Corpus differences are not causal estimates of change over time. App selection, platform evolution and capture method all differ between the two datasets and cannot be separated with these data alone.",
    "AndroidControl covers 833 apps chosen to support task demonstrations, which is a narrower and probably better-maintained population than Rico's broad 2017 crawl of 9,384 apps. That alone would push the newer corpus's coverage upward."
  ]
